            "id": 104334,
            "time": "2026-11-18T04:11:46Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "creation_time": "2026-11-18T04:11:46Z",
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "bug_id": 19339,
            "text": "## Summary\n\nOn Windows, `toupper()` and `tolower()` turn every character above U+FFFF after a string's first into a different one: `toupper(\"a\\U0001F600\")` returns U+1F7D8 instead of the emoji. Fixes a reproducible bug: wrong results, Windows only.\n\n## Details\n\nWhere `wchar_t` is 16 bits, `utf8towcs4()` in `src/main/util.c` completes each high surrogate with `utf8toucs32(*p, s)`, so the low half is computed from the start of the string `s` instead of the current character `t`. This dates from r79717; with a 32-bit `wchar_t` the branch is never taken. Seen in R 4.6.1 and R-devel on Windows 11; patch tested on a Windows build of r90925.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `utf8towcs4-low-surrogate-repro.R`; prints the code points after `toupper()`, `65 128984 128984` instead of `65 128512 128591`.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `utf8towcs4-low-surrogate.diff`; passes `t`, and adds a test to `tests/reg-tests-1e.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/511, where CI results can be seen.",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0
          },
          {
